\section{Simulation Setup and Execution}

\subsection{Physical Configuration}
We model a binary galaxy cluster merger inspired by 1E~0657-558 (the Bullet Cluster) at
redshift $z = 0.296$. The system consists of a primary cluster and a sub-cluster with
masses
\[
M_1 = 1.2 \times 10^{15} M_\odot, \qquad
M_2 = 1.5 \times 10^{14} M_\odot,
\]
each initialized with Hernquist dark matter profiles and hydrostatic $\beta$-model
intracluster gas distributions. The initial infall velocity is
\[
v_{\mathrm{infall}} = 3000~\mathrm{km/s} \quad (M \approx 3.2),
\]
with an impact parameter of $b = 120~\mathrm{kpc}$.

\subsection{Numerical Domain and Resolution}
The computational domain spans $8.0~\mathrm{Mpc}^3$ with 8 AMR refinement levels.
Each AMR patch contains $16^3$ active cells with 2-cell ghost halos (20$^3$ total),
stored in a 144-byte/cell Structure-of-Arrays (SoA) layout. At peak load, 39{,}321
active patches are resident in GPU VRAM.

\subsection{Solver Stack}
Time evolution is performed with:
\begin{itemize}
\item 3D HLLC-MHD flux solver (X, Y, Z directions),
\item Constrained Transport enforcing $\nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} = 0$,
\item SSP-RK3 symplectic integrator,
\item AMR refluxing at coarse–fine interfaces.
\end{itemize}
Self-gravity is included via a Poisson solver, and cosmological expansion is modeled
in comoving coordinates with Hubble drag terms $H(a)$.

\subsection{Execution Parameters}
The Bullet Cluster benchmark is evolved for
\[
T_{\mathrm{sim}} = 1.2~\mathrm{Gyr}
\]
over $1.42 \times 10^7$ integration timesteps. CUDA-aware MPI distributes AMR patches
across ranks, with non-blocking halo exchanges and cryptographically signed HDF5
frame output at selected checkpoints.